{"type":"message","id":"6817bc88","parentId":"2d3b98ba","timestamp":"2026-04-07T11:00:21.118Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_pk4MgCIY4GDFzSbZ4UkNhjqr|fc_0fffa0d689d6d8830169d4e3c504a88191865d28e67ad398a3","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: slm-dermatology\ndescription: Query a small language model (SLM) endpoint with dermatology expertise by asking a focused question about patient health data stored in records, skin symptoms, lesion descriptions, rash history, dermatology imaging context, or dermatology-relevant follow-up needs. Before each inference, first load the dermatology adapter with the fixed /node/load-adapter payload, then perform the query. Use when the agent needs a compact dermatology-specialist model pass over record-grounded or clearly provided skin-related context, and the SLM output should be processed rather than forwarded blindly.\n---\n\n# SLM Dermatology\n\nUse this skill to ask the dermatology SLM a focused question about patient data or clearly stated conversation context that is relevant to skin symptoms, lesions, rashes, dermatology images, or dermatology follow-up, then process the answer in the calling agent.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the task is within dermatology scope.\n   - Use this skill for skin-related interpretation, summarization, pattern spotting, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded dermatology questions.\n   - Prefer this skill when the user’s question concerns lesions, rashes, pigmentation changes, inflammatory skin disease, dermatology imaging context, or skin-focused differential support.\n   - Do not use it for unrelated non-dermatology requests.\n\n2. Build a focused question for the SLM.\n   - Write a single clear dermatology question.\n   - Ground the question in retrieved records, uploaded-image context already established by the agent, or clearly stated conversation facts.\n   - Keep it concise and specific.\n   - Do not invent findings, diagnoses, timelines, or morphology details.\n   - Good examples:\n     - `Based on this lesion description and image summary, which dermatology features are most concerning and what follow-up is most appropriate?`\n     - `From this patient record, what findings most strongly support inflammatory dermatitis rather than an infectious rash?`\n     - `What dermatology-focused differential diagnoses best fit this chronic pruritic plaque history?`\n     - `Which missing skin-history details would matter most before interpreting this pigmented lesion?`\n\n3. Load the dermatology adapter before every inference.\n   - Always do the adapter-load step immediately before the chat query.\n   - Run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_slm_dermatology.py \"<question>\"\n```\n\n   - The script first sends this payload to the adapter-loading endpoint:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"tinyllama\",\n  \"adapter_path\": \"adapters/derma_v1.0\",\n  \"mode\": \"derma\"\n}\n```\n\n   - Adapter endpoint:\n\n```text\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8007/node/load-adapter\n```\n\n   - It then sends the inference payload:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"<question>\"\n}\n```\n\n   - Chat endpoint:\n\n```text\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8007/chat\n```\n\n4. Read the response.\n   - Prefer a clean text answer.\n   - Accept common shapes such as `answer`, `Answer`, `response`, `message`, or raw text.\n   - If the endpoint returns nested JSON encoded as a string, extract the useful answer text when possible.\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, keep the best raw text and say so briefly in your own reasoning.\n\n5. Process the SLM answer in the calling agent.\n   - Do not treat the SLM output as the final user-facing answer by default.\n   - Use it as an input to the agent’s own reasoning, synthesis, or explanation.\n   - Cross-check it against the actual record or conversation context already available.\n   - Preserve uncertainty and avoid overstating confidence.\n   - If clinically relevant, highlight missing dermatology history, red flags, or next-step questions.\n   - Treat the output as supportive specialty inference, not as a confirmed diagnosis.\n\n## Output pattern\n\nReturn a response that includes:\n\n- **SLM finding**: the key content from the model answer, cleaned up if needed\n- **Agent interpretation**: the calling agent’s processed interpretation grounded in the available context\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when relevant\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: slm-dermatology\\ndescription: Query a small language model (SLM) endpoint with dermatology expertise by asking a focused question about patient health data stored in records, skin symptoms, lesion descriptions, rash history, dermatology imaging context, or dermatology-relevant follow-up needs. Before each inference, first load the dermatology adapter with the fixed /node/load-adapter payload, then perform the query. Use when the agent needs a compact dermatology-specialist model pass over record-grounded or clearly provided skin-related context, and the SLM output should be processed rather than forwarded blindly.\\n---\\n\\n# SLM Dermatology\\n\\nUse this skill to ask the dermatology SLM a focused question about patient data or clearly stated conversation context that is relevant to skin symptoms, lesions, rashes, dermatology images, or dermatology follow-up, then process the answer in the calling agent.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Confirm the task is within dermatology scope.\\n   - Use this skill for skin-related interpretation, summarization, pattern spotting, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded dermatology questions.\\n   - Prefer this skill when the user’s question concerns lesions, rashes, pigmentation changes, inflammatory skin disease, dermatology imaging context, or skin-focused differential support.\\n   - Do not use it for unrelated non-dermatology requests.\\n\\n2. Build a focused question for the SLM.\\n   - Write a single clear dermatology question.\\n   - Ground the question in retrieved records, uploaded-image context already established by the agent, or clearly stated conversation facts.\\n   - Keep it concise and specific.\\n   - Do not invent findings, diagnoses, timelines, or morphology details.\\n   - Good examples:\\n     - `Based on this lesion description and image summary, which dermatology features are most concerning and what follow-up is most appropriate?`\\n     - `From this patient record, what findings most strongly support inflammatory dermatitis rather than an infectious rash?`\\n     - `What dermatology-focused differential diagnoses best fit this chronic pruritic plaque history?`\\n     - `Which missing skin-history details would matter most before interpreting this pigmented lesion?`\\n\\n3. Load the dermatology adapter before every inference.\\n   - Always do the adapter-load step immediately before the chat query.\\n   - Run:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/query_slm_dermatology.py \\\"<question>\\\"\\n```\\n\\n   - The script first sends this payload to the adapter-loading endpoint:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"model\\\": \\\"tinyllama\\\",\\n  \\\"adapter_path\\\": \\\"adapters/derma_v1.0\\\",\\n  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"derma\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n   - Adapter endpoint:\\n\\n```text\\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8007/node/load-adapter\\n```\\n\\n   - It then sends the inference payload:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"<question>\\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n   - Chat endpoint:\\n\\n```text\\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8007/chat\\n```\\n\\n4. Read the response.\\n   - Prefer a clean text answer.\\n   - Accept common shapes such as `answer`, `Answer`, `response`, `message`, or raw text.\\n   - If the endpoint returns nested JSON encoded as a string, extract the useful answer text when possible.\\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, keep the best raw text and say so briefly in your own reasoning.\\n\\n5. Process the SLM answer in the calling agent.\\n   - Do not treat the SLM output as the final user-facing answer by default.\\n   - Use it as an input to the agent’s own reasoning, synthesis, or explanation.\\n   - Cross-check it against the actual record or conversation context already available.\\n   - Preserve uncertainty and avoid overstating confidence.\\n   - If clinically relevant, highlight missing dermatology history, red flags, or next-step questions.\\n   - Treat the output as supportive specialty inference, not as a confirmed diagnosis.\\n\\n## Output pattern\\n\\nReturn a response that includes:\\n\\n- **SLM finding**: the key content from the model answer, cleaned up if needed\\n- **Agent interpretation**: the calling agent’s processed interpretation grounded in the available context\\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when relevant\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8wBJGU5Q7cjyLk6hTz05dAXh|fc_0fffa0d689d6d8830169d4e3c504bc81918a4f73be415a404d","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/scripts/query_slm_dermatology.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom urllib import error, request\n\nBASE_URL = \"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8007\"\nLOAD_ADAPTER_ENDPOINT = f\"{BASE_URL}/node/load-adapter\"\nCHAT_ENDPOINT = f\"{BASE_URL}/chat\"\nLOAD_ADAPTER_PAYLOAD = {\n    \"model\": \"tinyllama\",\n    \"adapter_path\": \"adapters/derma_v1.0\",\n    \"mode\": \"derma\",\n}\n\n\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return body.strip()\n\n    if isinstance(parsed, str):\n        return parsed.strip()\n\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n    for key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n        value = parsed.get(key)\n        if value is not None:\n            if isinstance(value, str):\n                text = value.strip()\n                try:\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict):\n                        for nested_key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n                            nested_value = nested.get(nested_key)\n                            if nested_value is not None:\n                                return str(nested_value).strip()\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    pass\n                return text\n            return json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    data = parsed.get(\"data\")\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        for key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n            value = data.get(key)\n            if value is not None:\n                return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n\ndef post_json(url: str, payload: dict, timeout: int) -> str:\n    req = request.Request(\n        url,\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\"),\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Request to {url} failed: {e}\") from e\n\n\ndef load_adapter(timeout: int) -> str:\n    return post_json(LOAD_ADAPTER_ENDPOINT, LOAD_ADAPTER_PAYLOAD, timeout)\n\n\ndef call_endpoint(question: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\n    load_adapter(timeout)\n    body = post_json(CHAT_ENDPOINT, {\"question\": question}, timeout)\n    return extract_answer(body)\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Load the dermatology adapter and query the dermatology SLM endpoint\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"question\", help=\"Dermatology question grounded in records or known context\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=45)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.question, timeout=args.timeout)\n    print(answer)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"ERROR: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/scripts/query_slm_dermatology.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nimport argparse\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\nfrom urllib import error, request\\n\\nBASE_URL = \\\"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8007\\\"\\nLOAD_ADAPTER_ENDPOINT = f\\\"{BASE_URL}/node/load-adapter\\\"\\nCHAT_ENDPOINT = f\\\"{BASE_URL}/chat\\\"\\nLOAD_ADAPTER_PAYLOAD = {\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"tinyllama\\\",\\n    \\\"adapter_path\\\": \\\"adapters/derma_v1.0\\\",\\n    \\\"mode\\\": \\\"derma\\\",\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\\n    try:\\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n        return body.strip()\\n\\n    if isinstance(parsed, str):\\n        return parsed.strip()\\n\\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n    for key in (\\\"answer\\\", \\\"Answer\\\", \\\"response\\\", \\\"message\\\"):\\n        value = parsed.get(key)\\n        if value is not None:\\n            if isinstance(value, str):\\n                text = value.strip()\\n                try:\\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict):\\n                        for nested_key in (\\\"answer\\\", \\\"Answer\\\", \\\"response\\\", \\\"message\\\"):\\n                            nested_value = nested.get(nested_key)\\n                            if nested_value is not None:\\n                                return str(nested_value).strip()\\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n                    pass\\n                return text\\n            return json.dumps(value, indent=2)\\n\\n    data = parsed.get(\\\"data\\\")\\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\\n        for key in (\\\"answer\\\", \\\"Answer\\\", \\\"response\\\", \\\"message\\\"):\\n            value = data.get(key)\\n            if value is not None:\\n                return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\\n\\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n\\ndef post_json(url: str, payload: dict, timeout: int) -> str:\\n    req = request.Request(\\n        url,\\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n        headers={\\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\"},\\n        method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    try:\\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\\n            return resp.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\\n        detail = e.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}: {detail}\\\") from e\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Request to {url} failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n\\n\\ndef load_adapter(timeout: int) -> str:\\n    return post_json(LOAD_ADAPTER_ENDPOINT, LOAD_ADAPTER_PAYLOAD, timeout)\\n\\n\\ndef call_endpoint(question: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\\n    load_adapter(timeout)\\n    body = post_json(CHAT_ENDPOINT, {\\\"question\\\": question}, timeout)\\n    return extract_answer(body)\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\\n        description=\\\"Load the dermatology adapter and query the dermatology SLM endpoint\\\"\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"question\\\", help=\\\"Dermatology question grounded in records or known context\\\")\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--timeout\\\", type=int, default=45)\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n\\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.question, timeout=args.timeout)\\n    print(answer)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    try:\\n        main()\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        print(f\\\"ERROR: {exc}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        sys.exit(1)\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YoPfOCYzZDbTEzIbJlYbemlm|fc_0fffa0d689d6d8830169d4e3c504c88191bbfcad4d0e09e328","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/references/prompt-template.md","content":"# Dermatology SLM question template\n\nUse this shape when turning retrieved patient records, lesion descriptions, rash history, or already-established image context into one focused dermatology question for the SLM.\n\n```text\nPatient / dermatology context:\n- Patient id: <known or omitted>\n- Main skin concern: <known facts only>\n- Lesion / rash description: <known morphology, distribution, duration, symptoms>\n- Relevant history / treatments / triggers / images: <known facts only>\n- Important uncertainties or missing data: <if relevant>\n\nQuestion for SLM:\n<one clear dermatology question grounded in the available context>\n```\n\nGuidance:\n- Keep the final question focused and answerable.\n- Base it only on retrieved records or clearly stated conversation context.\n- Do not invent morphology, diagnoses, timing, or response-to-treatment details.\n- Prefer one strong dermatology question over several weak ones.\n- The calling agent should interpret the returned answer instead of relaying it blindly.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-dermatology/references/prompt-template.md\",\"content\":\"# Dermatology SLM question template\\n\\nUse this shape when turning retrieved patient records, lesion descriptions, rash history, or already-established image context into one focused dermatology question for the SLM.\\n\\n```text\\nPatient / dermatology context:\\n- Patient id: <known or omitted>\\n- Main skin concern: <known facts only>\\n- Lesion / rash description: <known morphology, distribution, duration, symptoms>\\n- Relevant history / treatments / triggers / images: <known facts only>\\n- Important uncertainties or missing data: <if relevant>\\n\\nQuestion for SLM:\\n<one clear dermatology question grounded in the available context>\\n```\\n\\nGuidance:\\n- Keep the final question focused and answerable.\\n- Base it only on retrieved records or clearly stated conversation context.\\n- Do not invent morphology, diagnoses, timing, or response-to-treatment details.\\n- Prefer one strong dermatology question over several weak ones.\\n- The calling agent should interpret the returned answer instead of relaying it blindly.\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":175,"output":2143,"cacheRead":16768,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19086,"cost":{"input":0.0004375,"output":0.032145,"cacheRead":0.0041919999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0367745}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775559581070}}
